--   Artin approximation library, file 04: Artin approximation for K[x_1..x_n] at the origin and at a rational point of a finite-type algebra (artinApproxAt)
-- statement:
--   Part 4 of 4 of a library proving Artin's approximation theorem at a rational point (M. Artin 1969, Theorem 1.10, étale-neighbourhood form): for a perfect field $K$, a finite-type $K$-algebra $A$ and a $K$-point $\chi : A \to K$, a solution in the $(\ker\chi)$-adic completion $\hat{A}$ of a finite polynomial system over $A$ gives a solution with the same residues in an étale neighbourhood of $\chi$. Everything is stated in Mathlib terms (`MvPolynomial`, `MvPowerSeries`, `AdicCompletion`, `Algebra.Etale`, `Algebra.TensorProduct`). Imports `Def_RPLib_FX_ArtinApprox_03`. Contents, in dependency order:
--
--   * the Jacobian datum in nested form and the $B'$-side of the induction step;
--   * `AA.all`: Artin approximation for $K[x_1, \dots, x_n]$ at the origin, for every $n$ ($K$ perfect);
--   * a presentation $A = K[x]/J$ centred at the point $\chi$, the completed presentation $\hat\pi : K[[x]] \to \hat{A}$, its surjectivity and its kernel $J \cdot K[[x]]$;
--   * `artinApproxAt`: Artin approximation at a $K$-rational point of a finite-type algebra over a perfect field.
-- source:
--   M. Artin, Algebraic approximation of structures over complete local rings, Publ. Math. IHÉS 36 (1969), 23–58; J.-C. Tougeron, Idéaux de fonctions différentiables, Springer (1972); H. Matsumura, Commutative Ring Theory, Cambridge University Press (1986), Chapters 8 and 10

